IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pca-types`

-- Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, Part 3 (ss 5 to 14), s 2 (the two defined terms the offences turn on) and ss 18(2), 21(2), 26, 27, 28,
-- 29 to 31, 32(2) (the offences outside Part 3).
-- Source: source/PCA1960.txt lines 98 to 164 (s 2), 504 to 694 (Part 3), 795 to 798, 873 to 880, 965 to 1032, 1035 to 1042.
--
-- The question this module answers: IS THIS AN OFFENCE UNDER THE ACT, AND WHAT IS THE MOST IT CAN COST?  Each offence section is one
-- rule over a record of facts.  Where the Act presumes (s 8) or deems (s 9) an element, the rule takes the presumption's outcome as a
-- BOOLEAN input, so the section 8 presumption is computed once (`the presumption of section 8 operates`) and a reviewer can see
-- where it enters each of ss 5 and 6.
--
-- "Corruptly" is the Act's word and the Act does not define it; it is a fact about the accused (`the accused acted corruptly`) and the
-- encoding does not decide it.  Every maximum below is a MAXIMUM: the Act fixes no minimum for any offence in it.

§ `2. Interpretation: gratification and agent`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 2 'gratification' (a) to (e)"
GIVEN g IS A `Gratification Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is a gratification` IF
        g's `the thing is money or a gift, loan, fee, reward, commission, valuable security or other property or interest in property of any description, movable or immovable`
    OR  g's `the thing is an office, employment or contract`
    OR  g's `the thing is a payment, release, discharge or liquidation of a loan, obligation or other liability whatsoever, in whole or in part`
    OR  g's `the thing is any other service, favour or advantage of any description whatsoever, including protection from a penalty or disability or from disciplinary or penal action, or the exercise or the forbearance from the exercise of a right or an official power or duty`
    OR  g's `the thing is an offer, undertaking or promise of anything within the other four paragraphs`

-- "agent" means any person employed by or acting for another, and includes a trustee, administrator and executor, and a person serving
-- the Government or under any corporation or public body; and "for the purposes of section 8 includes a subcontractor and any person
-- employed by or acting for such subcontractor".
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 2 'agent'"
GIVEN a IS AN `Agency Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an agent` IF
        a's `the person was employed by or acting for another`
    OR  a's `the person was a trustee, administrator or executor`
    OR  a's `the person was serving the Government or was under a corporation or public body`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 2 'agent', last words"
GIVEN a IS AN `Agency Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an agent for the purposes of section 8` IF
        `the person is an agent` a
    OR  a's `the person was a subcontractor, or employed by or acting for a subcontractor`

§ `8. Presumption of corruption in certain cases`

-- 8: where in any proceedings against a person for an offence under section 5 or 6 it is PROVED that a gratification has been paid or
-- given to or received by a person in the employment of the Government, a department or a public body, by or from a person or agent of a
-- person who has or seeks to have any dealing with the Government, a department or a public body, that gratification "shall be deemed to
-- have been paid or given and received corruptly as an inducement or reward as hereinbefore mentioned unless the contrary is proved".
-- The presumption supplies two elements of ss 5 and 6, that the gratification was given corruptly and that it was an inducement or
-- reward of the kind each section names; it does not supply that the thing is a gratification, or that it was in fact paid or received,
-- which are proved first.  The intermediary, if the dealing is not the payer's own, is an agent in the extended sense of section 2.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 8"
GIVEN p IS A `Presumption Facts`, intermediary IS AN `Agency Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the presumption of section 8 operates` IF
        p's `the gratification was paid or given to, or received by, a person in the employment of the Government or any department of the Government or of a public body`
    AND (   p's `the gratification was paid or given by, or received from, a person who has or seeks to have any dealing with the Government or any department of the Government or any public body`
         OR (   p's `the gratification was paid or given by, or received from, an agent of a person who has or seeks to have any dealing with the Government or any department of the Government or any public body`
            AND `the person is an agent for the purposes of section 8` intermediary))
    AND NOT p's `the contrary is proved`

§ `5. Punishment for corruption`

-- 5(a) and (b) are two limbs of one offence (one punishment clause).  Each needs: the act (solicit or receive or agree to receive; or give
-- or promise or offer), a gratification, and that it was given corruptly as an inducement to, reward for, or on account of, anything
-- in limb (i) any person's doing or forbearing in any matter, or (ii) a member, officer or servant of a public body's doing or forbearing
-- in a matter in which the public body is concerned.  "By himself or by or in conjunction with any other person" and "for himself or for any
-- other person" widen who acts and who benefits and add no element.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 5, the words after each of (a)(ii) and (b)(ii) (the purpose limbs)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 5 Facts`, presumed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gratification was corruptly an inducement or reward of the kind section 5 names` IF
        presumed
    OR  (   f's `the accused acted corruptly`
        AND (   f's `the gratification was an inducement to, reward for, or on account of, any person doing or forbearing to do anything in respect of any matter or transaction whatsoever, actual or proposed`
             OR f's `the gratification was an inducement to, reward for, or on account of, a member, officer or servant of a public body doing or forbearing to do anything in respect of any matter or transaction whatsoever, actual or proposed, in which the public body is concerned`))

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 5(a)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 5 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`, presumed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 5(a) is made out` IF
        f's `the accused solicited or received, or agreed to receive, a gratification for himself or herself or for any other person`
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND `the gratification was corruptly an inducement or reward of the kind section 5 names` f presumed

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 5(b)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 5 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`, presumed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 5(b) is made out` IF
        f's `the accused gave, promised or offered a gratification to any person, whether for the benefit of that person or of another person`
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND `the gratification was corruptly an inducement or reward of the kind section 5 names` f presumed

§ `6. Punishment for corrupt transactions with agents`

-- 6(a): an AGENT corruptly accepts or obtains, or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain, from any person a gratification as an inducement
-- or reward for an act in relation to his principal's affairs or business (or for showing or forbearing to show favour or disfavour).
-- 6(b): ANY PERSON corruptly gives or agrees to give or offers a gratification to an AGENT for the same.  6(c) is not about gratification:
-- a false, erroneous or defective receipt, account or document, knowingly given to an agent, or knowingly used by an agent with intent to
-- deceive the principal, in which the principal is interested and which to the giver's knowledge is intended to mislead.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 6, the inducement or reward words of (a) and (b)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 6 Facts`, presumed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gratification was corruptly an inducement or reward of the kind section 6 names` IF
        presumed
    OR  (   f's `the accused acted corruptly`
        AND f's `the gratification was an inducement or reward for doing or forbearing to do, or for having done or forborne to do, an act in relation to the principal's affairs or business, or for showing or forbearing to show favour or disfavour to any person in relation to the principal's affairs or business`)

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 6(a)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 6 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`, accused IS AN `Agency Facts`, presumed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 6(a) is made out` IF
        `the person is an agent` accused
    AND f's `the agent accepted or obtained, or agreed to accept or attempted to obtain, from any person, a gratification for himself or herself or for any other person`
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND `the gratification was corruptly an inducement or reward of the kind section 6 names` f presumed

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 6(b)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 6 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`, recipient IS AN `Agency Facts`, presumed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 6(b) is made out` IF
        f's `the accused gave, agreed to give or offered a gratification to an agent`
    AND `the person is an agent` recipient
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND `the gratification was corruptly an inducement or reward of the kind section 6 names` f presumed

-- 6(c), first limb: any person knowingly gives to an agent; second limb: an agent knowingly uses with intent to deceive his principal.
-- Both: the document is one in which the principal is interested, contains a statement false, erroneous or defective in a material
-- particular, and the statement is, to the accused's knowledge, intended to mislead the principal.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 6(c)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 6 Facts`, accused IS AN `Agency Facts`, recipient IS AN `Agency Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 6(c) is made out` IF
        (   (   f's `the accused knowingly gave an agent a receipt, account or other document`
            AND `the person is an agent` recipient)
         OR (   f's `the accused, being an agent, knowingly used with intent to deceive the principal a receipt, account or other document`
            AND `the person is an agent` accused))
    AND f's `the principal is interested in the document`
    AND f's `the document contains a statement which is false or erroneous or defective in a material particular`
    AND f's `the statement is, to the accused's knowledge, intended to mislead the principal`

§ `9. Acceptor of gratification to be guilty notwithstanding that purpose not carried out, etc.`

-- 9(1): where in proceedings against an agent for an offence under 6(a) it is proved that he corruptly accepted, obtained or agreed to
-- accept or attempted to obtain a gratification, having reason to believe or suspect that it was offered as an inducement or reward for
-- an act or favour in relation to his principal's affairs or business, he is guilty "notwithstanding" that he did not have the power,
-- right or opportunity, accepted without intending to do so, did not in fact do so, or that the act was not in relation to his
-- principal's affairs.  9(2) is the same for the giver under 6(b), having reason to believe or suspect that the agent had the power, right
-- or opportunity and that the act was in relation to the principal's affairs.  The four "notwithstanding" facts are fields so that a
-- reviewer and a test can see that they are not read.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 9(1)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 9 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`, accused IS AN `Agency Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 6(a) is made out by section 9(1)` IF
        `the person is an agent` accused
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND f's `the agent corruptly accepted, obtained or agreed to accept, or attempted to obtain, a gratification`
    AND f's `the accused had reason to believe or suspect that the gratification was offered as an inducement or reward for doing or forbearing to do an act, or for showing or forbearing to show favour or disfavour to a person, in relation to the principal's affairs or business`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 9(2)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 9 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`, recipient IS AN `Agency Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 6(b) is made out by section 9(2)` IF
        `the person is an agent` recipient
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND f's `the accused corruptly gave, agreed to give or offered a gratification to an agent`
    AND f's `the accused had reason to believe or suspect that the agent had the power, right or opportunity to do, show or forbear, and that the act, favour or disfavour was in relation to the principal's affairs or business`

§ `10, 11, 12. Withdrawal of tenders; bribery of a Member of Parliament; bribery of a member of a public body`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 10(a)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 10 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 10(a) is made out` IF
        f's `the accused offered a gratification to a person who had made a tender for a contract`
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND f's `the accused did so with intent to obtain the contract from the Government or a public body`
    AND f's `the contract was for performing work, providing a service, doing anything, or supplying an article, material or substance`
    AND f's `the gratification was an inducement or a reward for the tenderer's withdrawing the tender`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 10(b)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 10 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 10(b) is made out` IF
        f's `the accused solicited or accepted a gratification as an inducement or a reward for withdrawing a tender made by the accused for that contract`
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 11(a)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 11 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11(a) is made out` IF
        f's `the accused offered a gratification to a Member of Parliament`
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND f's `the gratification was an inducement or reward for the Member's doing or forbearing to do an act in his or her capacity as a Member`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 11(b)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 11 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11(b) is made out` IF
        f's `the accused, being a Member of Parliament, solicited or accepted a gratification`
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND f's `the gratification was an inducement or reward for the Member's doing or forbearing to do an act in his or her capacity as a Member`

-- 12: the three purposes in (a)(i), (ii) and (iii) are alternatives; (b) refers to them as "any such act, or any such abstaining".
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 12(a)(i), (ii), (iii)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 12 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gratification was for one of the purposes section 12 names` IF
        f's `the gratification was an inducement or reward for the member's voting or abstaining from voting at a meeting of the public body in favour of or against a measure, resolution or question submitted to it`
    OR  f's `the gratification was an inducement or reward for the member's performing or abstaining from performing, or aid in procuring, expediting, delaying, hindering or preventing the performance of, an official act`
    OR  f's `the gratification was an inducement or reward for the member's aid in procuring or preventing the passing of a vote or the granting of a contract or advantage in favour of any person`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 12(a)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 12 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 12(a) is made out` IF
        f's `the accused offered a gratification to a member of a public body`
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND `the gratification was for one of the purposes section 12 names` f

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 12(b)"
GIVEN f IS A `Section 12 Facts`, g IS A `Gratification Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 12(b) is made out` IF
        f's `the accused, being a member of a public body, solicited or accepted a gratification`
    AND `the thing is a gratification` g
    AND `the gratification was for one of the purposes section 12 names` f

§ `29, 30, 31. Abetment, attempts, conspiracy`

-- Each is "deemed to have committed the offence and shall be liable ... to be punished with the punishment provided for that offence".  The
-- meanings of "abets" and "criminal conspiracy" are the Penal Code 1871's (sg/penal-code-1871); they are facts here.  29(b) reaches an act
-- outside Singapore done for a principal residing in Singapore, which would be an offence under the Act if committed in Singapore.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 29(a) and (b), 30, 31"
GIVEN i IS AN `Inchoate Offence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused is deemed to have committed the offence by section 29, 30 or 31` IF
        i's `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission of an offence under this Act`
    OR  i's `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission outside Singapore of an act, in relation to the affairs or business or on behalf of a principal residing in Singapore, which if committed in Singapore would be an offence under this Act`
    OR  i's `the accused attempted to commit an offence punishable under this Act`
    OR  i's `the accused was a party to a criminal conspiracy, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, to commit an offence under this Act`

§ `Offences outside Part 3: ss 18(2), 21(2), 26, 27, 28, 32(2)`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 18(2)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Investigation Offence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 18(2) is made out` IF
        i's `an order of the Public Prosecutor under section 18(1) authorises the officer to investigate and to require disclosure or production`
    AND i's `the accused failed to disclose the information or to produce the accounts, documents or articles to the person so authorised`

-- 21(2): "wilfully neglects or fails so to comply" with a notice sent under 21(1), which the Public Prosecutor may send only in the course of
-- an investigation or proceedings into or relating to an offence by a person in the service of the Government, a department or a public body
-- under the Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871 (or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one).  The duty to
-- comply is "notwithstanding the provisions of any written law or any oath of secrecy to the contrary": no fact about secrecy is read.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 21(1) and (2)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Investigation Offence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 21(2) is made out` IF
        i's `a written notice of the Public Prosecutor under section 21(1) was sent to the accused in the course of an investigation or proceedings into an offence by a person in the service of the Government or of a department or of a public body`
    AND i's `the offence investigated is an offence under this Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy to commit, attempt to commit or abetment of one`
    AND i's `the accused wilfully neglected or failed to comply with the notice within the time specified in it`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 26(a) to (d)"
GIVEN s IS A `Section 26 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 26 is made out` IF
        s's `the accused refused the Director or an officer authorised to enter or search access to a place`
    OR  s's `the accused assaulted, obstructed, hindered or delayed the Director or an officer in effecting an entrance he or she is entitled to effect under the Act, or in the execution of a duty or power under the Act`
    OR  s's `the accused failed to comply with a lawful demand of the Director or an officer in the execution of his or her duty under the Act`
    OR  s's `the accused refused or neglected to give information which might reasonably be required of him or her and which he or she had it in his or her power to give`

-- 27 creates a duty and no offence of its own; the offence for breaching it is section 26(d) (neglect to give information), whose
-- punishment is the section 26 punishment.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 27"
GIVEN s IS A `Section 27 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is legally bound to give the information` IF
        s's `the person was required by the Director or an officer to give information`
    AND s's `the information is on a subject which it is the duty of the Director or that officer to inquire into under this Act`
    AND s's `it is in the person's power to give the information`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 28(a) and (b)"
GIVEN s IS A `Section 28 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 28 is made out` IF
        s's `the accused knowingly gave or caused to be given false or misleading information relating to the commission of an offence under this Act or under section 165, 213, 214 or 215 of the Penal Code 1871`
    OR  s's `the accused knowingly gave or caused to be given to the Director or a special investigator any other false or misleading information`

-- 32(2): a public officer to whom a gratification is corruptly given or offered "shall arrest the person who gives or offers" it and make
-- him over to the nearest police station; failing to do so "without reasonable excuse" is the offence.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 32(2)"
GIVEN s IS A `Section 32(2) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 32(2) is made out` IF
        s's `a gratification was corruptly given or offered to the public officer`
    AND NOT s's `the public officer arrested the person who gave or offered the gratification and made the person over to the nearest police station`
    AND NOT s's `the public officer had a reasonable excuse for not doing so`

§ `The Penal Code sections the Act names`

-- Three differently drawn lists, because the Act draws three: ss 17(1)(a) and 28(a) name "section 165 or ... sections 213 to 215"
-- (28(a): "165, 213, 214, or 215"); ss 20(1), 21(1), 22, 24(1) and 35(1) name "sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215".  A reader who assumes they
-- are one list will believe section 28(a) reaches the bribery sections 161 to 164, which it does not.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 17(1)(a) and 28(a)"
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the Penal Code sections named in sections 17(1)(a) and 28(a)` MEANS
    LIST "165", "213", "214", "215"

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 20(1), 21(1), 22(1) and (2), 24(1), 35(1)"
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the Penal Code sections named in sections 20, 21, 22, 24 and 35` MEANS
    LIST "161", "162", "163", "164", "165", "213", "214", "215"

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 17(1)(a) and 28(a)"
GIVEN section IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Penal Code section is one that sections 17(1)(a) and 28(a) name` IF
    NOT null (filter (GIVEN named YIELD named EQUALS section) `the Penal Code sections named in sections 17(1)(a) and 28(a)`)

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 20, 21, 22, 24 and 35"
GIVEN section IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Penal Code section is one that sections 20, 21, 22, 24 and 35 name` IF
    NOT null (filter (GIVEN named YIELD named EQUALS section) `the Penal Code sections named in sections 20, 21, 22, 24 and 35`)

§ `5, 6, 7 and the others. Punishment`

-- Sections 5, 6, 10, 11 and 12 carry a fine not exceeding $100,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 5 years (ss 5, 6) or 7 years (ss 10, 11,
-- 12) or both.  Section 7 raises the imprisonment ceiling of an offence under section 5 or 6 from 5 to 7 years where the matter or
-- transaction was a contract or proposal for a contract with the Government, a department or a public body, or a subcontract to execute
-- work comprised in such a contract; the fine ceiling is the same $100,000.  All figures are maxima.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 7"
GIVEN c IS A `Government Contract Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the matter or transaction was a government or public body contract, or a subcontract` IF
        c's `the matter or transaction was a contract or a proposal for a contract with the Government or any department of the Government`
    OR  c's `the matter or transaction was a contract or a proposal for a contract with a public body`
    OR  c's `the matter or transaction was a subcontract to execute work comprised in such a contract`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 5, 6 (punishment clauses) and 7"
GIVEN c IS A `Government Contract Facts`
GIVETH A `Corruption Punishment`
`the ceiling for an offence under section 5 or 6` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the matter or transaction was a government or public body contract, or a subcontract` c THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 100000, 84
           OTHERWISE `Corruption Punishment` OF 100000, 60

-- The maximum imprisonment is in months so that "6 months" and "one year" are exact.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 5, 6, 7, 10, 11, 12, 18(2), 21(2), 26, 28 and 32(2)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence under the Act`, c IS A `Government Contract Facts`
GIVETH A `Corruption Punishment`
`the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `Corruption by soliciting or receiving (section 5(a))` THEN `the ceiling for an offence under section 5 or 6` c
    WHEN `Corruption by giving, promising or offering (section 5(b))` THEN `the ceiling for an offence under section 5 or 6` c
    WHEN `Agent accepting or obtaining a gratification (section 6(a))` THEN `the ceiling for an offence under section 5 or 6` c
    WHEN `Giving a gratification to an agent (section 6(b))` THEN `the ceiling for an offence under section 5 or 6` c
    WHEN `False receipt, account or document given to or used by an agent (section 6(c))` THEN `the ceiling for an offence under section 5 or 6` c
    WHEN `Offering a gratification for the withdrawal of a tender (section 10(a))` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 100000, 84
    WHEN `Soliciting or accepting a gratification for withdrawing a tender (section 10(b))` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 100000, 84
    WHEN `Offering a gratification to a Member of Parliament (section 11(a))` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 100000, 84
    WHEN `Member of Parliament soliciting or accepting a gratification (section 11(b))` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 100000, 84
    WHEN `Offering a gratification to a member of a public body (section 12(a))` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 100000, 84
    WHEN `Member of a public body soliciting or accepting a gratification (section 12(b))` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 100000, 84
    WHEN `Failure to disclose information or produce documents to an authorised person (section 18(2))` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 2000, 12
    WHEN `Failure to comply with a notice of the Public Prosecutor (section 21(2))` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 10000, 12
    WHEN `Obstruction of search and failure to give information (section 26)` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 10000, 12
    WHEN `False or misleading information (section 28)` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 10000, 12
    WHEN `Public officer failing to arrest the giver of a gratification (section 32(2))` THEN `Corruption Punishment` OF 5000, 6

-- 29, 30, 31: the abettor, attempter or conspirator "shall be liable on conviction to be punished with the punishment provided for that
-- offence": the same record.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 29, 30, 31"
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence under the Act`, c IS A `Government Contract Facts`
GIVETH A `Corruption Punishment`
`the punishment for abetting, attempting or conspiring to commit the offence` MEANS
    `the punishment for the offence` o c

§ `13. When penalty to be imposed in addition to other punishment`

-- 13(1): where a court convicts a person of an offence "committed by the acceptance of any gratification", then if the gratification is a
-- sum of money or its value can be assessed, the court SHALL, in addition to any other punishment, order the person to pay as a penalty a sum
-- equal to the amount of the gratification or, in the court's opinion, its value, recoverable as a fine.  The offences committed by
-- acceptance are those whose act is to solicit, receive, accept or obtain: 5(a), 6(a), 10(b), 11(b), 12(b).
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 13(1)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence under the Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is committed by the acceptance of a gratification` IF
        o EQUALS `Corruption by soliciting or receiving (section 5(a))`
    OR  o EQUALS `Agent accepting or obtaining a gratification (section 6(a))`
    OR  o EQUALS `Soliciting or accepting a gratification for withdrawing a tender (section 10(b))`
    OR  o EQUALS `Member of Parliament soliciting or accepting a gratification (section 11(b))`
    OR  o EQUALS `Member of a public body soliciting or accepting a gratification (section 12(b))`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 13(1)"
GIVEN s IS A `Section 13 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must order a penalty under section 13(1)` IF
        s's `the person is convicted of an offence committed by the acceptance of a gratification in contravention of the Act`
    AND (   s's `the gratification is a sum of money`
         OR s's `the value of the gratification can be assessed`)

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 13(1)"
GIVEN s IS A `Section 13 Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the penalty under section 13(1) in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the court must order a penalty under section 13(1)` s THEN JUST (s's `the amount of the gratification, or in the court's opinion its value, in dollars`)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- 13(2): where the person is charged with 2 or more offences for the acceptance of gratification, is convicted of one or some, and the
-- others are taken into consideration under section 148 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 for sentence, the court MAY increase the
-- penalty by an amount not exceeding the total amount or value of the gratification in the charges so taken into consideration.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 13(2)"
GIVEN s IS A `Section 13 Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greatest increase of the penalty the court may make under section 13(2) in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF     `the court must order a penalty under section 13(1)` s
              AND s's `the other offences taken into consideration under section 148 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 were offences for the acceptance of gratification in contravention of the Act`
           THEN s's `the total amount or value of the gratification specified in the charges for the offences taken into consideration, in dollars`
           OTHERWISE 0

§ `14. Principal may recover amount of secret gift`

-- 14(1): the principal may recover as a civil debt the amount or money value of a gratification given in contravention of the Act to an
-- agent, from the agent or from the giver; "no conviction or acquittal of the defendant ... shall operate as a bar".  No fact about a
-- conviction or acquittal is read.  14(2) saves the principal's other rights and adds no condition.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 14(1)"
GIVEN s IS A `Section 14 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal may recover the amount as a civil debt` IF
        s's `a gratification has, in contravention of this Act, been given by a person to an agent`
    AND s's `the plaintiff is the principal`
    AND s's `the defendant is the agent or the person who gave the gratification`
